Falsifies `intrusive_queue::verification::appending_joins_two_queues_in_order`.

The defect: `append` stops emptying the queue it took the nodes from. The lines read as
tidying, because every node already sits on the first queue and the join is right, so the first
queue's order and count stay correct. The second queue still names the moved nodes as its head
and tail, so its next push links a node behind one that now belongs to the other queue, and both
queues walk the same nodes.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that the second queue is empty after the append,
whenever it held a node.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -399,8 +399,6 @@
         // Wrapping: the two counts are of distinct live nodes, so their sum is a count of distinct
         // live nodes too, which never reaches `usize::MAX`, as in `push_back`.
         self.len = self.len.wrapping_add(other.len);
-        other.head = None;
-        other.tail = None;
         other.len = 0;
     }
 
